/* ===================== *
 *      Runemaster       *
 * ===================== */
@1201 = ~runemaster~
@1202 = ~Runemaster~
@1203 = ~Runemaster:

The Runemaster is a Fighter who has mastered the ancient art of runecraft, inscribing powerful magical symbols that influence the battlefield and empower those who fight within their presence.
Through five distinct runic inscriptions, the Runemaster can strengthen allies, protect his companions, devastate enemies, reveal hidden threats and disrupt hostile magic.

The Runemaster is a versatile frontline Fighter whose strength lies in preparation, positioning and adaptability rather than exceptional raw damage.

Advantages:
- 1st level: May use the Rune Carving ability twice per day, gaining an additional use every 4 levels thereafter.

Rune Carving:
The Runemaster inscribes a magical rune at a selected location, creating a stationary magical field with a 10ft radius that affects creatures within its area.
As the Runemaster gains experience, <PRO_HISHER> runes become more powerful and he learns to craft additional runes:

Rune of Warding:
The Runemaster inscribes a protective symbol that surrounds nearby allies with an aura of magical protection, keeping them safe from harm.
Allies within the rune gain the following benefits:
- 1st level: +3 bonus to AC, +1 bonus to all saving throws.
- 9th level: +4 bonus to AC, +2 bonus to all saving throws, +5% physical damage resistance.
- 18th level: +5 bonus to AC, +2 bonus to all saving throws, +10% physical damage resistance.

Rune of Might:
The Runemaster inscribes a symbol of strength and martial prowess, empowering nearby allies and improving their ability to strike their enemies.
Allies within the rune gain the following benefits:
- 1st level: +2 bonus to THAC0 and physical damage.
- 9th level: +3 bonus to THAC0 and physical damage, +5% critical hit chance.
- 18th level: +4 bonus to THAC0 and physical damage, +10% critical hit chance.

Rune of Ruin (available from level 6):
The Runemaster inscribes a destructive symbol that releases repeated pulses of magical energy, damaging and weakening enemies caught within its influence.
Hostile creatures within the rune suffer the following effects:
- 6th level: 2d6 magical damage per round.
- 9th level: 3d6 magical damage per round, -20% movement speed.
- 18th level: 4d6 magical damage per round, -30% movement speed.

Rune of Revelation (available from level 9):
The Runemaster inscribes an ancient symbol of perception, allowing nearby allies to detect hidden threats and protecting them against supernatural ambushes.
This rune affects both allies and hostile creatures:
- 9th level: Hostile creatures are revealed, allies gain increased vision range.
- 18th level: Allies are additionally immune to backstab.

Rune of Nullification (available from level 12):
The Runemaster inscribes a powerful anti-magic symbol that protects nearby allies from hostile magic.
Allies within the rune gain the following benefits:
- 12th level: +3 bonus to saving throws vs spell, +15% magic resistance.
- 18th level: +4 bonus to saving throws vs spell, +30% magic resistance, +20% magic damage resistance.

Each rune stays on the battlefield for 5 rounds.
Only one rune may be active at a time. Creating a new rune replaces the previous one.

- 10th level: The Runemaster's growing mastery allows <PRO_HIMHER> to inscribe runes of greater potency. Their symbols now radiate power far beyond their carved boundaries, expanding the reach of all runes from 10 to 15 feet.
- 15th level: Gain the Runic Resonance passive ability. 

Runic Resonance:
The Runemaster has learned to channel the power of <PRO_HISHER> runes directly into <PRO_HISHER> body and weapons.
While standing within the area of <PRO_HISHER> runes, <PRO_HESHE> gains additional personal benefits according to the inscribed rune.

These effects only benefit the Runemaster himself and do not affect nearby allies:

Rune of Warding:
- +20% bonus to elemental resistances, immunity to poison and disease.

Rune of Might:
- +1/2 bonus to APR, immunity to fear, +2 bonus to saving throws vs death.

Rune of Ruin:
- +1d6 magical damage with each melee attack, gain a 10% chance to briefly stun struck targets.

Rune of Revelation: 
- instantly cast True Sight.

Rune of Nullification:
- instantly cast Globe of Invulnerability, Spell Shield and Spell Immunity: Abjuration. 

Disadvantages:
- race restricted to dwarves.
- May only achieve Mastery (3 points) in weapons.
- Cannot use longbows, shortbows, or crossbows.~ 

@1204 = ~Rune Carving~
@1205 = ~Rune Carving
Select one of your available runes and inscribe it at a chosen location. The rune creates a stationary field whose effects depend on the rune and your level. All inscriptions share a limited pool of daily uses.~ 
@1206 = ~Rune of Warding~
@1207 = ~Rune of Warding
Inscribes a protective field at the chosen location. Nearby allies gain physical damage resistance for 3 rounds; the strength of the protection increases with your level.~ 
@1208 = ~Rune of Might~
@1209 = ~Rune of Might
Inscribes a battlefield rune at the chosen location. Nearby allies gain improved accuracy and melee damage for 3 rounds; the bonuses improve with your level.~ 
@1210 = ~Rune of Nullification~
@1211 = ~Rune of Nullification
Inscribes an anti-magic rune at the chosen location. When activated, it dispels enemy combat protections in its area. Enemies in the field must save vs. Spell or suffer spellcasting failure for 3 rounds.~ 
@1212 = ~Rune of Ruin~
@1213 = ~Rune of Ruin
Inscribes a destructive rune at the chosen location. It pulses once per round for 3 rounds, damaging enemies in a medium area with magical energy and weakening their defenses at higher levels.~ 
@1214 = ~Rune of Sight~
@1215 = ~Rune of Sight
Inscribes a rune at the chosen location that reveals invisible enemies and protects allies from backstabs for 5 rounds. Its detection improves as you gain levels.~ 
